\TODO[Genome]

Protocols generating epigenetic data have been extended to the single cell level.
Chromatin accessibility on single cell genomes can be measured using single-cell Assay for Transposase-Accessible Chromatin using Sequencing (scATAC-Seq, \inlinecite[buenrostro2013]).
DNA methylation can be measured using the recently developed single cell Cleavage Under Targets and Tagmentation (scCUT&Tag, \inlinecite[kaya-okur2019]).
For analysis of scRNA-Seq data combined with both kinds of data, \n{epiScanpy} offers a \n{scanpy}-integrated workflow \cite[danese2019].
Since it uses the current version of \n{AnnData}, its API will benefit from the upcoming multi-modal extension of \n{AnnData}.

